{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "00ZB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-topology-site}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93713f4492b827a1c34b7ba2164eee31cfe43cecde2f1a4a4cfaad605253f297", "source_text": "The topology defined by a site", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5b724d685fc4a4750fe65f846b6aeadf47eb980a6dc7effcc8a1abd0ff1640e", "unit_id": "tag:00ZB:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00ZB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Cov}_1(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Cov}_2(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\text{Cov}_1(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Cov}_2(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$J$", "MATH_0009": "$J$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-refine-same-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-topology-and-topos}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3752c799dab50775807964ab01745021d9c3e9df2e44f4aa1087372dc701ffb8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25fb1c5da7a441e25a2ca2bcfa169f8b4efd4926350cd9be464ae54d57099f58", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSuppose that <MATH_0001> is a category, and suppose that\n<MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003>\nare sets of coverings that define the structure of a site\non <MATH_0004>. In this situation it can happen that\nthe categories of sheaves (of sets) for <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> are the same, see for example\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIt turns out that the category of sheaves on <MATH_0007>\nwith respect to some topology <MATH_0008>\ndetermines and is determined by the topology <MATH_0009>.\nThis is a nontrivial statement which we will address later,\nsee Theorem <REF_0002>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nAccepting this for the moment it makes sense to study the\ntopology determined by a site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:388d817158423ba5a5324a9dd4753d225dcdc31b6b6c79cf3ecd2272e3b83de7", "unit_id": "tag:00ZB:prose-0001"}
